y net. If a payment had failed, you’d still have recourse. But if an electronic voting machine in a foreign country had a glitch, you’d have no recourse, no receipt, and no way to know—even if you were the voter whose vote was changed. **In short:** Your trust in payments is justified because the system is *designed to be reversible*. Voting cannot be reversible, so the same level of trust is not justified. It’s not about the technology being different—it’s about the rules of the game being completely opposite.
